    "q-6508": {
      "dom_id": "step-q6508",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Suppose there are $5$ different crayons. In how many possible ways can they be arranged?",
      "worked_solution": "There are $n=5$ crayons, so the number of possible arrangements is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5! & =5\\times 4\\times 3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $120$ ways of arranging $5$ crayons.",
