    "q-19899": {
      "dom_id": "step-q19899",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Michael goes to a restaurant and orders a sandwich, a salad, and a muffin. In how many different orders can he decide to eat his food?",
      "worked_solution": "There are $3$ foods, so there are $3!$ ways of ordering them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3! & =3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are 6 possible arrangements.",
