    "q-86869": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86869",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A railway train has $6$ passenger wagons. How many ways can $6$ conductors be distributed among the wagons if one conductor is assigned to each wagon?",
      "worked_solution": "There are $6$  conductors to arrange, so there are $6!$ ways of arranging them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6! & =6\\times 5\\times \\times 3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =720.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
